# Design guidelines — ZDMS_UPLOAD_FILES code-review deck

Goal: present 30 findings across 4 axes for a single ABAP program, prioritize,
and surface the run economics. Audience is SAP architects + EMs.

## Theme

- `Theme.DEFAULT`
- No custom images. No image blocks.
- Diagrams: `BlockProcess` for "Four parallel category checks" (slide 6) and
  for the "Recommended action order" (slide 23).
- No ConceptMap; the structure is matrix + prioritized list, not radial.

## Block styles (limit to 5 across the deck)

| Style | When to use |
|---|---|
| `BlockStyle.HERO_METRIC_ON_TOP` | Every severity overview slide (4 blocks: CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW), executive snapshot (slide 3), retro economics (slide 24). |
| `BlockStyle.SOLID_FILL` | Per-finding cards in the findings list grids (slides 9, 12, 15, 18, 19). Severity is encoded by the accent color (see below), not by an icon. |
| `BlockStyle.CALLOUT` | Verdict / footnote blocks (slide 14 "Verdict: rewrite, not patch"; slide 21 totals caption; slide 3 manual-review caption). |
| `BlockStyle.LEFT_ICON_AND_TITLE` | The 2-block "What it does / How it does it" on slide 5 and the 4-block retro lessons on slide 25. |
| `BlockStyle.TOP_ICON_AND_TITLE` | The 4-step BlockProcess slides (slides 6, 23). |

## Severity color convention

Use the same accent color for the same severity *everywhere* — readers should
recognize severity at a glance.

| Severity | Accent color | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| CRITICAL | `EPAMColor.Red` (dark slides) / `EPAMColor.Light_Red` (light slides) | Never visible on this deck (count = 0) but reserve the color so future runs render consistently. |
| HIGH | `EPAMColor.Orange` / `EPAMColor.Light_Orange` | Used on every overview + every HIGH finding card. |
| MEDIUM | `EPAMColor.Cyan` / `EPAMColor.Light_Teal` | |
| LOW | `EPAMColor.Gray` / `EPAMColor.Light_Gray` | Keep neutral — 16 LOW findings should not draw the eye away from HIGHs. |

Override `auto_color_rotation=False` on the per-finding BlockGrids and set
`accent_color` explicitly on each block to enforce the convention.

## Color usage on non-severity content

- Dark slides: `EPAMColor.Cyan` for primary, `EPAMColor.MintGreen` for
  contrast (Cover, Section Headers Dark, slide 22 verdict).
- Light slides: `EPAMColor.Light_Blue` for primary, `EPAMColor.Light_Teal`
  for contrast.

## Process style

- `BlockProcess`, horizontal, 4 steps each. Single accent color per process
  (no rotation). Use `EPAMColor.Light_Blue` on slide 6, `EPAMColor.Orange`
  on slide 23 (urgency cue).

## Layout notes

- Slide 21 "Findings heatmap" — implement as a `BlockGrid` of small
  `SIMPLE` cells in a 5-column × 5-row arrangement (header row + 4 category
  rows). Each cell is a one-line title (the count). Bold the HIGH column
  by using `EPAMColor.Orange` on those cells.
- Slide 18-19 each carry 8 LOW findings — 4 columns × 2 rows. Tight title,
  one-line content per card.

## Things to avoid

- No animations, transitions.
- No charts. Counts go into HERO_METRIC blocks or the matrix grid.
- No images.
- Block content ≤ 1 short paragraph or 3 bullets. If text wraps past 2 lines,
  shorten — never let blocks auto-resize to be much larger than their grid cell.
